            <ArticleTitle>Clinicopathologic correlates of common cancer pain syndromes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-78</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The development of a treatment strategy for the management of cancer pain is based on a patient evaluation that elucidates the pain syndrome and predominant pathophysiological mechanism responsible for the pain. Coupled with evaluation of pain intensity, and the extent of functional and emotional disturbance, this assessment facilitates appropriate selection of primary and analgesic therapies to address the problem of patient distress.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
